sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User<br/>(Wallet + own SSI agent)
    participant A as App<br/>(client + own SSI agent)
    participant C as CSS Server<br/>VcDidCommHttpHandler /<br/>AgentInitializer / AcpReader /<br/>PermissionBasedAuthorizer
    participant T as TTP<br/>(Trusted Third Party<br/>+ own SSI agent)

    rect rgb(230, 240, 255)
    note over U,A: DIDComm Exchange (OOB invitation generated by the app,<br/>wallet connects on demand during the flow)
    U->>A: DIDComm Exchange
    note over U: App authorized (for the User)
    note over A: User authorized (for the App)
    end

    rect rgb(255, 250, 230)
    note over U,C: HTTPS
    A->>C: HTTP GET resource<br/>(headers: didvc=true, agent=holder DID,<br/>client=app DID, issuer=issuer DID)
    C-->>A: 401 Unauthorized<br/>WWW-Authenticate: didcomm proofRequest=[base64url JSON VPR]
    note right of C: createDidcommAuthenticateHeader():<br/>nonce + presentationExchange VPR,<br/>nonce→domain stored server-side

    note over U,A: DIDComm (present-proof v2) — App collects the presentation from the User's wallet
    A->>U: Forward (signed/wrapped) proof request<br/>(App ↔ Wallet exchange)
    U-->>A: Verifiable Presentation<br/>(agent / issuer / client DIDs,<br/>proof over challenge=nonce)

    A->>C: [HTTP] GET resource<br/>(header: vp = [JSON VP])
    C->>C: validNonceAndDomain(vp) → challenge + domain match
    C->>C: VpChecker.verifyNew(vp) →<br/>Credentials[agent, issuer, client]
    note over A: App authorized (for the Verifier)
    note over U: User authorized (for the Verifier)
    C->>C: AcpReader: matcher on agent/issuer/client<br/>→ acl:Read and/or acl:NRRead<br/>PermissionBasedAuthorizer: mode granted

    alt 3a. Only acl:Read granted → serve directly
        C-->>A: 200 OK + plaintext resource
    else 3b. Only acl:NRRead granted → escrowed non-repudiable read
        note over C,T: Reserved DIDComm channel (opened on first use, reused)
        C->>T: DIDComm Exchange
        C->>C: Fetch resource content, encrypt it with<br/>a fresh symKey ⇒ encryptedMessage (DIDComm JWE),<br/>symKey encrypted for the TTP's recipient keys<br/>(encrypted_key inside the JWE recipients)
        C->>C: messageHash = sha256(resource content),<br/>symKey + pending context kept server-side<br/>(hash → connectionId / requesterDid / requestedResource)
        C->>C: attachNonRepudiationMaterial():<br/>hashCredential = NonRepudiableOrigin VC<br/>(CSS-signed, subject=requesterDid, signedHash)<br/>+ signatureFromCSS = JWS over messageHash
        C-->>A: [HTTP] encryptedresource header:<br/>encryptedMessage (JWE) + hash +<br/>hashCredential + signatureFromCSS<br/>(no key yet — stays escrowed at the CSS)
    end
    end

    rect rgb(255, 240, 240)
    note over U,C: 4. App signs the receipt (NRR)
    A->>A: Create and sign NRR<br/>(NonRepudiationDestination VC):<br/>issuer=app, subject=requesterDid,<br/>requestedResource, signedHash=messageHash

    alt 5a. Release via CSS (App stays with the server it already talked to)
        A->>C: [HTTP] GET resource<br/>(header: signedresource = [NRR JSON])
        C->>C: verifySignedResource(NRR) → verify VC signature,<br/>match signedHash / requesterDid / requestedResource<br/>against the pending context
        C->>C: jwsGraphService.storeVerifiedJws(...)<br/>(CSS-side non-repudiation evidence),<br/>escrowed key + pending context deleted
        C-->>A: [HTTP] keyfordecrypt header
    else 5b. Release via TTP (App goes straight to the escrow — alternative path)
        A->>T: [HTTP] checkResource(encryptedMessage, nrr)
        T->>T: Verify NRR signature + NRO consistency<br/>(hashCredential / signatureFromCSS vs hash),<br/>then decrypt the encrypted_key (JWE recipient)
        T-->>A: [HTTP] keyForDecrypt
    end

    note over U,A: 6. Deliver resource to the user
    A->>A: Decrypt encryptedMessage locally<br/>with keyForDecrypt → plaintext resource
    A-->>U: Deliver resource to the User<br/>(app-specific)
    end